<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "Hex Sudoku is Sudoku for one player. Fill the 9×9 grid so every row, every column and every 3×3 box holds the digits 1 to 9 once. Every grid is made new for your game and has one solution, which you can always reach without guessing. The fastest wins go into the ranking."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_keyboard}>{dgettext("help_games", "Controls")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_games", "Tap a square, or move with the arrows")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "— Choose it. Its row, column and box are highlighted, and so is every square with the same digit"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_games", "Tap a digit next to the grid, or press 1 to 9")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "— Write that digit in the square you chose. A digit turns grey next to the grid once all nine are in place"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_games", "The pencil, or N")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "— Switch between digits and notes. With the pencil on, a digit is written small, as a note. The same digit again removes it."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>
      {dgettext("help_games", "The eraser, %{delete} or %{backspace}",
        delete: "Delete",
        backspace: "Backspace"
      )}
    </strong>
     {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "— Clear the chosen square's digit or notes"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_games", "The light bulb, or H")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "— A hint: reveal the chosen square, or one at random when the chosen square is already correct"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>{dgettext("help_games", "The arrow, or Z")}</strong> {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "— Cancel your last move. A hint is not cancelled"
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_games", "Rules")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "A wrong digit turns red immediately and adds 30 seconds to your clock. A hint adds a minute."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "A correct digit removes that digit from the notes in its row, column and box."
    )}
  </li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "Hex Sudoku is the easy level. Hex Sudoku: Medium needs pairs and digits pointing out of a box, and Hex Sudoku: Hard an X-Wing, a Swordfish or an XY-Wing."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_games", "Score")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_games",
      "Points come only from a win: 10,000 divided by the minutes on your clock, mistakes and hints included. The faster you finish, the more points. If you end a game with End, it scores nothing."
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_joystick}>{dgettext("help_games", "Inspiration")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_games",
    "Sudoku first appeared in American puzzle magazines in the 1970s. It got its name in Japan in the 1980s and then spread to newspapers all over the world."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_games", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="feature-hex-mines">{dgettext("help_games", "Hex Mines")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="feature-retro-games">{dgettext("help_games", "Retro Games")}</.help_link>
</p>
